o  have a recovery  without a she covering she says a  different kind of downturn requires  a different kind of solution one that  focuses on the so-called caring economy  the often unpaid hours of work the  majority done by women to take care of  children the elderly and those unable to  look after themselves  rolling school and daycare shutdowns  have erased decades of employment gains  for women workers  early learning and child care has to be  the centerpiece  of the next budget from the first ever  female finance minister of canada  in the first ever self-declared feminist  government of canada  the liberals have promised to create a  national child care system  needed to help parents mostly women stay  or get back into the workforce  labor market analysts say tools to allow  workers to reskill will also help  and human resource experts are calling  on ottawa to create  incentives to help employers retain  women any types of you know through eap  through through different types of  programs through wellness programs  within the workplace  if employers can be provided with the  financial means  to provide these uh these supports  within the workplace  that would really go a long way men have  returned to the labor force more quickly  but nearly half a million women remain  unemployed one hundred thousand have  dropped out of the workforce  historically the longer they stay out  the more likely they are to stay out  permanently  reducing household income and spending  productivity and tax revenue  all a major drag on any hope of a  sustainable recovery  ann gaviola global news toronto  tomorrow marks the third anniversary of  the humboldt broncos bus crash and  tonight the team's hometown has unveiled  its vision  to honor the memory of the 16 people  killed there will be a roadside memorial  and a tribute center to showcase the  spirit of the nation  in the wake of the crash the city of  humboldt will launch a national campaign  to support the cost of construction  in 2018 the broncos team was on its way  to a game when it crashed into a truck  that had run a stop sign  the canucks versus the coronavirus up  next cover 19  checks vancouver's hockey team  the vancouver canucks are at the center  of a coveted 19 outbreak  17 players are on the nhl's protocol  list  that's more than half the team some  coaches have been hit hard too  the nhl insists the season isn't over  for the team  but as eric sorensen reports the cases  are still throwing a wrench  into the schedule for a while the  all-canadian division of the nhl looked  to be getting everything right  the season was proceeding almost  uninterrupted but now the vancouver  canucks have been brought to their knees  by covet 19  from netminder braden holtby to star  forward and captain beau horvath  close to 20 canucks players and coaches  are on the league's protocol list  some are thought to be quite sick adam  gaddet's wife is herself recovering and  tweeted last week  my hubby isn't in great shape but i'm  taking good care of him  first and foremost there is concern for  the health of the canucks  and their families across the league  obviously what's happening in vancouver  is a lot more than hockey so  you know we're obviously thinking you  know we're hoping that  everyone's doing all right there are  reports the more infectious variant  first seen in brazil  is involved potentially raising new  risks for the league we're now learning  uh this may make behaviors that were  previously  accepted and safe a little bit less safe  the nhl says it remains confident that  canucks will be able to complete their  season  the league began january 13th with a  56-game regular season to run till may  8th  then the playoffs were to start up to  march 20th more than two dozen us-based  games were postponed by kovid  with other games rescheduled but then  canada was hit  starting march 22nd four montreal  canadiens games were called off  and now for the vancouver canucks four  games have been postponed so far  and there may be more the nhl is now  extending the regular season to make up  games starting the week of may 10th  and the playoffs will be pushed back  from there there is speculation the  league may have to return to a bubble  like  last summer it's really incumbent upon  the canucks organization and the league  to really  ensure that that the situation is  tightened so that it doesn't spread and  become a much bigger problem  but what has happened to the canucks is  a cautionary tale for all of us  if that can affect someone of that  physical caliber you know none of us are  at this athletic level  all of us are at risk the serious  outbreak with the canucks comes in spite  of the league doing regular testing and  following stringent protocols  a sign that the next phase of the  pandemic may be riskier than first  imagined  eric sorensen global news toronto  and that is global national for this  monday night i'm robin gill  the signs of spring are cropping up in  many parts of the country and especially  in british columbia  so we'll leave you tonight with a sunset  flyby of these beautiful cherry blossoms  they're a staple of the vancouver  landscape at this time of year  thank you for watching donna friesen  will be back at the anchor desk tomorrow  and i'll see you on friday have a great  [Music]  [Applause]  night  you
 

